  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/3902e622-2dbd-4a10-b888-4c4780250e61-141.png\" style=\"width: 354px; height: 250px;\" /></p><p>We know that for making a triangle, we require three points, which are not on a line.</p><p>Here, we have total&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>14</mn></math>&nbsp;points out of which&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn></math>&nbsp;points&nbsp;respectively, on&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;are collinear.</p><p>Thus, the total Number of triangles formed</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>14</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>-</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>3</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>-</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>5</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>-</mo><mmultiscripts><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>3</mn><none></none><mprescripts></mprescripts><none></none><mn>6</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#183;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>14</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>364</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>333</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Hence, total number of triangles is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>333</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>",
    "image": null
